('127.51.d.15.A',3,'Pre-surgical care often includes:','["No monitoring", "Feeding a large meal", "Skipping exams", "Fasting the animal as directed and running pre-op blood work"]'::jsonb,3,'Fasting reduces vomiting under anesthesia; labs check readiness.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.A',4,'After surgery, owners are typically told to:','["Limit activity and watch the incision", "Skip medication", "Encourage jumping", "Remove the bandage right away"]'::jsonb,0,'Rest and incision monitoring support healing.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.B',3,'A scalpel is used to:','["Measure temperature", "Make incisions", "Hold a patient", "Clean teeth"]'::jsonb,1,'Scalpels cut tissue in surgery.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.B',4,'Hemostats are used to:','["Measure heart rate", "Hold the animal''s head", "Clamp blood vessels", "Cut hair"]'::jsonb,2,'Hemostats control bleeding by clamping vessels.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.C',3,'An autoclave sterilizes surgical packs using:','["Cold water", "Soap alone", "Dry air only", "Steam under pressure"]'::jsonb,3,'High-pressure steam kills microbes.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.C',4,'A sterile surgical pack should be opened:','["Without touching the sterile contents", "After sneezing on it", "On the floor", "With dirty hands"]'::jsonb,0,'Sterile technique prevents contamination.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.D',3,'Spaying is the surgical removal of a female animal''s:','["Teeth", "Reproductive organs", "Tail", "Ears"]'::jsonb,1,'An ovariohysterectomy prevents pregnancy.','original'),
('127.51.d.15.D',4,'Neutering a male animal is called:','["Declawing", "Biopsy", "Castration", "Spaying"]'::jsonb,2,'Castration removes the testicles.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.A',3,'An X-ray machine produces images using:','["Visible light only", "Sound waves only", "Magnets only", "Radiation passing through the body"]'::jsonb,3,'X-rays differ in absorption by bone and tissue.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.A',4,'Ultrasound creates images with:','["High-frequency sound waves", "Heat", "Radio stations", "X-rays"]'::jsonb,0,'Echoes of sound waves form moving images of soft tissue.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.B',3,'Staff taking X-rays should wear:','["Sandals", "Lead aprons and use dosimeter badges", "Jewelry", "Open shirts"]'::jsonb,1,'Lead blocks scatter radiation and badges track exposure.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.B',4,'The best way to limit radiation exposure is to:','["Stand in the beam", "Skip the apron", "Stay back and keep hands out of the beam", "Hold the animal by hand"]'::jsonb,2,'Distance and shielding reduce exposure.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.C',3,'Positioning for an X-ray is important because:','["It speeds up billing", "It prevents the need for restraint", "It makes no difference", "It affects the quality and usefulness of the image"]'::jsonb,3,'Correct positioning shows the body part clearly.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.C',4,'Sedation may be used for imaging to:','["Keep the animal still and reduce stress", "Make it bark more", "Heal the problem", "Replace the image"]'::jsonb,0,'Stillness gives better images and protects staff.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.D',3,'Which image would best show a fractured bone?','["A fecal float", "An X-ray", "A blood test", "A urine test"]'::jsonb,1,'Bones appear clearly on radiographs.','original'),
('127.51.d.16.D',4,'Which tool is best to view the heart''s moving chambers?','["Plain film X-ray alone", "A scale", "Ultrasound", "A thermometer"]'::jsonb,2,'Ultrasound shows real-time motion of soft tissues.','original'),
('127.51.d.17.A',3,'Antibiotics are used to treat:','["Broken bones", "Hunger", "Viral infections", "Bacterial infections"]'::jsonb,3,'Antibiotics act on bacteria, not viruses.','original'),
