('127.52.d.8.A',3,'Domestication of animals means:','["Capturing any wild animal once", "Releasing animals into the wild", "Selecting animals over generations to live with and serve people", "Banning animals"]'::jsonb,2,'Domestication is a long process of breeding for useful traits.','original'),
('127.52.d.8.A',4,'Dogs were among the first animals to be:','["Discovered on Mars", "Extinct", "Cloned", "Domesticated"]'::jsonb,3,'Dogs are descended from wolves and were domesticated long ago.','original'),
('127.52.d.8.B',4,'A change in the global food market, such as rising grain prices, can affect animal producers by:','["Raising feed costs", "Eliminating demand", "Removing all competition", "Lowering all prices"]'::jsonb,0,'Feed is a major cost, so grain price shifts matter.','original'),
('127.52.d.8.B',5,'A new export market for beef can:','["Reduce prices to zero", "Increase demand and prices for producers", "Eliminate farms", "End trade"]'::jsonb,1,'Greater demand typically raises prices.','original'),
('127.52.d.8.C',3,'A Hereford is a breed of:','["Poultry", "Swine", "Beef cattle", "Dairy goats"]'::jsonb,2,'Herefords are known for beef production.','original'),
('127.52.d.8.C',4,'When comparing breeds, producers look at:','["Colors only", "Names only", "Price of ink", "Traits such as growth, temperament, and adaptability"]'::jsonb,3,'Breed traits affect production and fit to environment.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.A',3,'Muscle cells and nerve cells differ because they:','["Have structures suited to different functions", "Do not exist", "Are identical", "Have no nuclei"]'::jsonb,0,'Specialized cells have specific forms.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.A',4,'A red blood cell is specialized to:','["Send nerve signals", "Carry oxygen", "Produce milk", "Digest food"]'::jsonb,1,'Hemoglobin carries oxygen.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.B',3,'Mitosis produces:','["One cell", "Four sex cells", "Two identical body cells", "No cells"]'::jsonb,2,'Mitosis is used for growth and repair.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.B',4,'Meiosis produces:','["More skin", "Muscle fiber", "Identical body cells", "Gametes with half the chromosomes"]'::jsonb,3,'Meiosis forms eggs and sperm with a half set.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.C',3,'Cell differentiation is the process by which:','["Cells become specialized for different jobs", "Cells stop dividing", "Cells become identical", "Cells die"]'::jsonb,0,'Differentiation forms tissues and organs.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.C',4,'Stem cells can:','["Only become blood", "Develop into several cell types", "Stop working", "Never change"]'::jsonb,1,'They are unspecialized and can differentiate.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.D',3,'The correct order from smallest to largest is:','["System, organ, tissue, cell", "Tissue, system, cell, organ", "Cell, tissue, organ, organ system", "Organ, cell, tissue, system"]'::jsonb,2,'Levels of organization build in complexity.','original'),
('127.52.d.9.D',4,'The stomach is an example of a(n):','["Tissue", "Molecule", "Cell", "Organ"]'::jsonb,3,'An organ is made of tissues working together.','original'),
('127.52.d.10.A',3,'Compared with dogs, cattle have:','["Hooves and a multi-part stomach", "Claws and one stomach", "Gills", "Wings"]'::jsonb,0,'Cattle are hoofed ruminants.','original'),
('127.52.d.10.A',4,'Horses differ from cattle in having:','["Gills", "A single-toed hoof and a simple stomach", "Four stomach compartments", "Horns always"]'::jsonb,1,'Horses are non-ruminant herbivores with a single digit hoof.','original'),
('127.52.d.10.B',3,'The function of the heart is to:','["Digest food", "Filter urine", "Pump blood through the body", "Make bile"]'::jsonb,2,'The heart circulates blood.','original'),
('127.52.d.10.B',4,'The kidneys are part of the:','["Endocrine system only", "Digestive system", "Skeletal system", "Urinary system"]'::jsonb,3,'They filter blood and produce urine.','original')
