('127.52.d.11.G',4,'Which feed is typically higher in protein?','["Corn stalks", "Straw", "Sawdust", "Alfalfa hay"]'::jsonb,3,'Alfalfa is a legume with high protein.','original'),
('127.52.d.11.H',3,'Alfalfa and clover are:','["Legume forages", "Grains", "Minerals", "Fertilizers"]'::jsonb,0,'Legumes are high in protein and fix nitrogen.','original'),
('127.52.d.11.H',4,'Bermudagrass is commonly used as:','["A bedding material only", "A warm-season forage", "A mineral", "A cold-season only"]'::jsonb,1,'It grows in hot weather and supplies grazing and hay.','original'),
('127.52.d.11.I',3,'Rotational grazing means:','["Leaving animals in one place forever", "Feeding only grain", "Moving animals among pastures to rest the land", "Never grazing"]'::jsonb,2,'Rest allows plants to regrow.','original'),
('127.52.d.11.I',4,'A benefit of rotational grazing is:','["Less forage", "More weeds always", "No benefits", "Improved pasture growth and reduced overgrazing"]'::jsonb,3,'Pasture health improves with rest periods.','original'),
